{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:01:07.752281Z","id":"93a0aa0902f2d0275f1e5fda4f17aee9b5f2255bd2067a5aa6bd3c4764b93e95","body":{"detail":"build computes `keep` (text, thinking or tool_uses non-empty) only after the whole file is read, and the merge places a kept turn ahead of every event whose watermark is past it. attach_tool_call (line 553) adds a function_call to the most recent assistant turn (last_assistant_turn_index, line 759), which can be an earlier assistant message with `content: []`. Reproduced with a temporary test: rollout = session_meta, turn_context, user message, assistant message with content [], event_msg token_count. Derived step ids: [session_meta, turn_context, codex-turn-0001, token_count]. Append one function_call line and derive again: [session_meta, turn_context, codex-turn-0001, codex-turn-0002, token_count]. The new codex-turn-0002 lands before token_count, and token_count's parent changes from codex-turn-0001 to codex-turn-0002. So the later derive does not start with the earlier one, which is the property this change sets out to give Codex (CHANGELOG.md, 'Turns and events become one ordered item stream'). Both repository fixtures (sample-codex-python.jsonl, compacted_session.jsonl) stay prefix-stable for every line prefix, so this needs an empty assistant message to trigger.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":388},"content_hash":"e63b7524bc26ea9a55d143957bade5123d5beb50b0c2045a7b2e5f6495d8dd00"},"suggested_fix":"Decide keep when the turn is pushed rather than at the end of the file. Either keep every assistant message turn (drop only turns that can never gain content), or have attach_tool_call open a new synthetic assistant turn when the latest assistant turn was empty at push time. Add a Codex test that derives every line prefix of a fixture and asserts each derive's step ids start with the previous derive's ids, like the Claude wire_order_roundtrip test.","summary":"Codex Builder::build drops an assistant turn that has no text yet, then puts it back when a later function_call fills it, so a growing rollout derives a step in the middle of the earlier derive's steps","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:01:07.760211Z","id":"5c0cba00858f9b66f79a4c24c80b2aaa57848ed1069a8075465f76b67ae177f2","body":{"detail":"Real rollouts often go user message -> reasoning -> function_call with no assistant message in between (see tests/fixtures/sample-codex-python.jsonl, where a reasoning line is followed directly by custom_tool_call apply_patch). last_assistant_turn_index (line 759) returns the most recent assistant turn of any round, so the tool call and its file mutations are recorded on an assistant step that comes before the user prompt that asked for them. Reproduced with a temporary test: round t1 = user 'hi', assistant 'answer one', task_complete; round t2 = turn_context, user 'second', reasoning, function_call exec_command. The exec_command lands on codex-turn-0002 ('answer one'), not in round t2. It also means appending to a rollout rewrites an earlier step's content (codex-turn-0002 grows a tool_use), even though step ids stay prefix-stable. main has the same attach logic.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":553},"end":{"line":564},"content_hash":"d246b52e67640d76a9f93a22de67e09f56ddf24a423bf52c681b9ed4e904de75"},"suggested_fix":"In attach_tool_call, reuse the latest assistant turn only when it belongs to the current round (group_id == current_round_id) and no user turn follows it; otherwise push a synthetic assistant turn at the current position.","summary":"Pre-existing on main: Codex attach_tool_call puts a round's function_call on the previous round's final assistant turn, which sits before that round's user turn","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:01:07.767711Z","id":"c01e4d953a79290824ef936bbc3f8932e1ba732d81fc836bd2ba93db16565b0b","body":{"detail":"The projector rebuilds session_meta, turn_context, token_count, agent_message, exec_command_end and patch_apply_end from turn fields. Nothing writes back a `compacted` line, even though the reader now keeps it as an event at its rollout position and tests/compaction_roundtrip.rs pins that position through derive -> extract. So a Codex session exported back to Codex (or a Claude session's events exported to Codex) still loses its compaction marker. Dropping events is pre-existing on main (main's loop at origin/main project.rs:184 also walked turns only). The new comment makes the loss look intentional and complete.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"047f792af109b2fe02e2e0804e94742da0f244d52317fc0b24cfaf1150a03684"},"suggested_fix":"Either write `compacted` (and other raw rollout events whose data is the original payload) back at their item position by walking view.items, or change the comment to list what is lost, e.g. 'events are dropped; session_meta/turn_context/token_count/exec_command_end/patch_apply_end are rebuilt from turns, `compacted` and unknown lines are lost'.","summary":"The new comment in Codex project_view says dropped events are re-derived from the turns, but `compacted`, `session_state`, `user_message` and unknown rollout lines are not re-derived and are lost on export","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:08:39.606031Z","id":"d5d0b9d8b56901508c7f622a062726c7268342ad0f986f01a6041c15104475b9","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/provider.rs:331-335 computes `keep` after the whole file is read; attach_tool_call (553-567) uses last_assistant_turn_index (759-764), which picks the empty assistant turn. Temporary test (since deleted): rollout session_meta, turn_context, user 'hi', assistant content [], token_count derives [session_meta, turn_context, codex-turn-0001, token_count(parent codex-turn-0001)]; after appending a function_call line it derives [session_meta, turn_context, codex-turn-0001, codex-turn-0002, token_count(parent codex-turn-0002)]. The later derive does not start with the earlier one. origin/main was not prefix-stable at all (it appended events after all turns, origin/main crates/toolpath-convo/src/derive.rs:339-421), so this is a gap in the new guarantee and concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"93a0aa0902f2d0275f1e5fda4f17aee9b5f2255bd2067a5aa6bd3c4764b93e95","summary":"confirmed: regression against this change's stated goal: an empty assistant message dropped by Codex Builder::build reappears mid-stream once a later function_call fills it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:08:39.606061Z","id":"c518eedc4359e8f73f9c1f89235e3b19abf96ff668ab1cb05841b0fa14dbe761","body":{"detail":"Temporary test (since deleted): round t1 = user 'hi', assistant 'answer one', task_complete; round t2 = turn_context, user 'second', reasoning, function_call exec_command. to_view items: codex-turn-0001 User 'hi'; codex-turn-0002 Assistant 'answer one' tools=[exec_command]; task_complete; turn_context; codex-turn-0003 User 'second'. So the tool call sits before the prompt that asked for it. Cause: last_assistant_turn_index at crates/toolpath-codex/src/provider.rs:759-764, used by attach_tool_call at 553. origin/main has the same code (origin/main provider.rs:513 and 719-724).","kind":"comment","references":"5c0cba00858f9b66f79a4c24c80b2aaa57848ed1069a8075465f76b67ae177f2","summary":"confirmed: pre-existing on main: Codex attach_tool_call puts round two's function_call on round one's assistant turn","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:08:39.606070Z","id":"36cae0447ccc9cfa7fa128e89d286f19a3189e18ba931223c880638f620e5b8c","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath-codex/src/project.rs:184-187 adds the comment and loops over view.turns() only; `grep -n 'compacted\\|Item::Event\\|view.items' crates/toolpath-codex/src/project.rs` returns nothing, so no `compacted` line is ever written. origin/main project.rs:184 also iterated turns only.","kind":"comment","references":"c01e4d953a79290824ef936bbc3f8932e1ba732d81fc836bd2ba93db16565b0b","summary":"confirmed: the new comment in Codex project_view says every dropped event is rebuilt from turns, but `compacted` lines are dropped and never rebuilt (the dropping is pre-existing on main; the comment is new)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
